From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 18:04:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] svc.startd: build without libbe and libfmevent

TIER 4 -- NOT UPSTREAMABLE, KEEP LOCAL. This removes functionality to avoid
two dependency chains, and upstream should not take it as written. The shape
a real submission would need is this same pair of macros wired to a build-time
knob and *defaulted on*, so that a normal gate build is unchanged and only an
explicitly reduced configuration opts out; that is not what this does -- here
the macros are simply never defined.

svc.startd links `-lbe` and `-lfmevent` for one call site each, and each drags
in a stack far larger than the feature:

  * `libbe` is used once, `be_get_boot_args()` in `graph.c`, and pulls in
    `-lzfs -lficl-sys -lefi -lzfsbootenv -linstzones -luuid -ldevinfo` -- the
    whole ZFS stack, in a VM whose entire premise is a root hsfs with no ZFS
    at all.

  * `libfmevent` publishes FMA "state-transition" telemetry, and pulls in
    `-ltopo` and its plugins.

Neither is load-bearing for starting a service, and both call sites already
have supported failure paths, which is what makes omitting them equivalent to
something the code already does rather than a new behaviour:

  * `be_get_boot_args()` is reached only when `halting == AD_FASTREBOOT`, and
    on failure startd already sets `halting = AD_BOOT` and warns "Failed to
    get fast reboot arguments. Falling back to regular reboot." The
    `#elif defined(__x86)` arm added here does exactly that, with a message
    naming the real reason. Fast reboot is meaningless under qemu regardless.

  * `dgraph_state_transition_notify()` exists only to publish that one event.
    Its sole other effects are the `stev_ct_*` counters, which are documented
    as "indicative only" and which nothing reads. A failed publish is already
    just `log_framework(LOG_DEBUG, ...)`, so a build that never publishes is
    the same outcome as one that never succeeds.

The call sites are guarded rather than the `-l` flags merely dropped, so that
a build without these libraries fails to compile the references rather than
surprising the next person at link time.

Assisted-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/Makefile | 13 ++++---------
 usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/graph.c  | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/Makefile b/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/Makefile
index b599e57c51..ace9be4935 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/Makefile
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/Makefile
@@ -100,16 +100,11 @@ LDLIBS += \
 	-luutil
 
 #
-# While svc.startd only searches for libfmevent, which is in
-# $(ROOT)/lib/fm, when resolving dependencies it needs to know to search
-# for those in $(ROOT)/usr/lib/fm. However, we don't need a runpath
-# because libfmevent has that properly set already, but it doesn't help
-# us during the build.
+# libbe and libfmevent are deliberately not linked here; see the
+# SMF_HAVE_LIBBE and SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT guards in graph.c. Neither is
+# defined, so neither library is referenced.
 #
-LDLIBS_i386 +=	-lbe
-LDLIBS +=	$(LDLIBS_$(MACH)) -L$(ROOT)/lib/fm -lfmevent \
-		-L$(ROOT)/usr/lib/fm
-LDFLAGS +=	-R/lib/fm
+LDLIBS +=	$(LDLIBS_$(MACH))
 
 FILEMODE = 0555
 
diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/graph.c b/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/graph.c
index bd272bb8d4..c9b3e3e64a 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/graph.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/svc/startd/graph.c
@@ -145,7 +145,9 @@
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#ifdef SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT
 #include <fm/libfmevent.h>
+#endif	/* SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT */
 #include <libscf.h>
 #include <libscf_priv.h>
 #include <librestart.h>
@@ -162,9 +164,9 @@
 #include <sys/statvfs.h>
 #include <sys/uadmin.h>
 #include <zone.h>
-#if defined(__x86)
+#if defined(__x86) && defined(SMF_HAVE_LIBBE)
 #include <libbe.h>
-#endif	/* __x86 */
+#endif	/* __x86 && SMF_HAVE_LIBBE */
 
 #include "startd.h"
 #include "protocol.h"
@@ -3612,7 +3614,7 @@ do_uadmin(void)
 	 * print warning and fall back to regular reboot.
 	 */
 	if (halting == AD_FASTREBOOT) {
-#if defined(__x86)
+#if defined(__x86) && defined(SMF_HAVE_LIBBE)
 		if (be_get_boot_args(&fbarg, BE_ENTRY_DEFAULT) == 0) {
 			mdep = (uintptr_t)fbarg;
 		} else {
@@ -3623,6 +3625,16 @@ do_uadmin(void)
 			uu_warn("Failed to get fast reboot arguments.\n"
 			    "Falling back to regular reboot.\n");
 		}
+#elif defined(__x86)	/* !SMF_HAVE_LIBBE */
+		/*
+		 * Built without libbe, so the default boot environment's boot
+		 * arguments cannot be read. This is the same outcome as
+		 * be_get_boot_args() failing, which the branch above already
+		 * falls back from.
+		 */
+		halting = AD_BOOT;
+		uu_warn("Fast reboot configured, but this svc.startd was "
+		    "built without libbe.\nFalling back to regular reboot.\n");
 #else	/* __x86 */
 		halting = AD_BOOT;
 		uu_warn("Fast reboot configured, but not supported by "
@@ -4668,6 +4680,20 @@ static void
 dgraph_state_transition_notify(graph_vertex_t *v,
     restarter_instance_state_t old_state, restarter_str_t reason)
 {
+#ifndef SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT
+	/*
+	 * Built without libfmevent. Everything this function does is in
+	 * service of publishing one FMA "state-transition" event; the only
+	 * other effects are the indicative stev_ct_* counters, which nothing
+	 * reads. Publishing already fails softly -- the error path below is a
+	 * log_framework(LOG_DEBUG, ...) and nothing more -- so omitting it is
+	 * the same outcome as a publish that never succeeds.
+	 */
+	(void) v;
+	(void) old_state;
+	(void) reason;
+}
+#else	/* SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT */
 	restarter_instance_state_t new_state = v->gv_state;
 	int stn_transition, maint;
 	int from, to;
@@ -4750,6 +4776,7 @@ dgraph_state_transition_notify(graph_vertex_t *v,
 		nvlist_free(attr);
 	}
 }
+#endif	/* SMF_HAVE_LIBFMEVENT */
 
 /*
  * Find the vertex for inst_name.  If it doesn't exist, return ENOENT.
